<title>PHILIPPINES: Indonesian bank to establish Philippine office.</title>
<headline>Indonesian bank to establish Philippine office.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine central bank said on Thursday it had approved the licence of Bank Internasional Indonesia (BII) to operate a representative office in the country.</p>
<p>BII, the third largest private bank in Indonesia, is the 29th foreign bank to establish a representative office in the Philippines.</p>
<p>BII is the third Indonesian bank to operate in the country. The first two are Bank Dagang Nasional Indonesia and PT LippoBank.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
